[Music]  I just noticed during the last break via  Twitter multiple reporters covering the  Dolphins pointing out that Brian Flores  the new coach in Miami has canceled the  final mandatory minicamp practice they  will do conditioning work instead you  know Chris I was talking about this  earlier in the week on the PFT p.m.  podcast I don't understand how coaches  complain that they don't have enough  time in the offseason to work with their  players and then they cancel practices  unless like always plan to cancel a  practice is like a camaraderie thing or  just to give the players a you know a  reward for working hard so no matter how  many practices there are they'll always  cancel one I just still have a hard time  with this idea that they don't think  they have enough practice time and then  they voluntarily sacrifice mandatory  practice time no I I hear you Mike it is  a little weird I know I was a part of a  few instances like that where I you know  whether I was playing or even then I got  done playing more yeah I mean oh gosh we  don't have enough time wish we had more  time with these guys and then yeah the  last day of practice gets cutoff and you  go well ma'am we just you know let it  six hours of more preparation for the  season get away but I think it's it's  more than that it's more than just the  one day that the coaches are concerned  with I think realistically you know  first thing is as you know we know  anybody knows that's following football  the coaches are in heart attack mode  right now anyways they're just going oh  gosh I hope everybody stays healthy and  we don't lose somebody by the time  training camp gets here so they get  towards the end of the finish line and  they just want to get there and get to  the get to training camp unscathed I  think the other thing with what the  coaches are saying I think they're  crying getting to this point gun okay  this one practice isn't gonna matter you  know I think they want more teachable  moments throughout the offseason whether  players got to get there earlier in the  offseason or the rules are just a little  different to where you can have more  meaning time in the classroom or  walkthroughs on the field more teachable  moments like that I think that are  ultimately really frustrating coaches  and right on cue multiple reporters  pointing out the Jets have canceled yeah  their final practice of the three day  mandatory minicamp they're holding an  off-site team activity so whether  they're going bowling or going to the  movies or whether playing laser tag or  paintball or whatever  does that really help III think it does  but you lived it right does it how much  does it help bond players together when  you get away from work and you go do  something like that as a group it is uh  it does work it's it's shockingly  awesome really because it's you know  again NFL players are grown men you know  when you get out of the locker room and  the day's work is done you kind of go to  your different ways you know everybody's  got their own little clique a little bit  as like oh the DBS might hang out  together or defensive guys so not  everybody's all together when you have  these camaraderie moments makes you get  on the team bus you might sit next to a  group of guys you normally don't and you  start to find out about guys and it  starts to be you know you start to get  ba you know bonds and trust and get to  know someone guys you might not know on  the roster and some situations that you  know you're both unfamiliar with and I  do I really do think it is very  important for players and it has great  value within the locker room and really  just the overall Mon you know state of  the franchise to keep everybody kind of  normal sane and realizing this is fun  and we're human beings what's the best  team activity that that you were ever  involved oh gosh well I mean Jeff Fisher  always had you know great you know  Thanksgiving Day pranks and things like  that where he'd send the rookies to go  get turkeys and Thanksgiving and they  thought they were bringing back turkeys  to the facility to help like a great  cause and there would be a bag of ice in  the box and they'd be like oh no I  didn't bring the turkey back like some  of that stuff was great as far as  jokester but Gruden did a great job of  like bringing us to the bowling alley  and having it all set up bowling alley  all for the team we got food and drinks  set up and we'd go over there for three  or four hours and have a little  competition set it up too you know we  had teams and everybody was mixed  together there was just some of the best  times in my life really a lot of laughs  and a lot of a lot of good moments and  that's how you create the environment  where guys have each other's phone  numbers they communicate with each other  a separate and apart from work yes and  they just they they feel a greater  connection to each other and a greater  desire to make sure that they're not  letting each other down and that's all  about crafting a team and I think in  this day and age in the  fell it's critical because every year  the team is dramatically different so  you have your steps every season to  bring your guys together you're right  it's not the old days you know a lot of  these guys you know you could be the  quarterback of a football team and they  sign a free-agent safety and here you  are five weeks into you know offseason  program and you go damn I even really  talked to this guy I don't even know if  he's married he's got kids whatever it  is and sometimes it's these little  gatherings that oh wow I do like this  guy hey maybe we'll have you and the  wife over for a barbecue in a few days  and that's how it kind of all starts and  that's part of football football family  Mike football weighs family we're doing  hey take off Chris you've earned it yes  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

